      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The name Södermalm first appeared in 1288 in a letter from Bishop Anund of Strängnäs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S%C3%B6dermalm",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Once known as a slum, Södermalm today thrives as a hub of bohemian culture and diverse cultural amenities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S%C3%B6dermalm",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Björngårdsteatern, opened in the 17th century, was perhaps Scandinavia's first theatre and stood on Södermalm.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
